          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উপচে পড়া — upôche pôṛā — \"to overflow; to brim over\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কলটা বন্ধ না করলে বালতি থেকে জল উপচে পড়বে। Kôlṭā bôndhô nā kôrle bālti theke jôl upôche pôṛbe. If you don't turn off the tap, the water will overflow the bucket."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): সেই দুধ উপচে পড়ল, sei dudh upôche pôṛlô."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said of milk boiling over too, as in the past form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উপচে পড়া (upôche pôṛā) joins উপচে, the -এ form of a verb that CDIAL lists as Bengali upacāna, \"to boil over, to overflow\", under a reconstructed utpacyatē, \"boils over\" (CDIAL 1808), to পড়া, \"to fall\": the water falls over the rim as it spills."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
